A||||5||artherd||Where to buy these? (racecar parts)||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||12-17-2001||05:06 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://abacus.sj.ipixmedia.com/abc/M28/5e0a7ccdeab989047452e02bac/i-1.JPG"> <P>Not the rod ends, I'm already going with NHBB all stainless ends (with these cool end dust seals too from BakerPrecision...)<P>But where the heck do I get the aluminum threaded rods?!<P>I've looked everywhere!  Can't even figure out what these puppies are called exactly...<P>It's so embaresing!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-17-2001||07:56 AM||||Use threaded steel. It's called 'ALL THREAD' and should be able to be purchased at your better hardware stores.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Daleford||12-17-2001||08:15 AM||||Called strut rod tubes or trailing arms. [from my old stockcar racing days] U.B.Machine, In. has oodles of them. They are always at the Daytona Feb show. Nice folks. 219 493 3381   or <A HREF="http://www.ubmachine.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ubmachine.com</A>   <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||12-17-2001||04:46 PM||||A good race shop should be able to make them for you. A shop near here has bulk lengths of aluminum bar, they cut it to the length you need and tap the male and female threads in the ends.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Lizzy||12-17-2001||09:40 PM||||I own a sprint car.  Those rods are used extensively on my car.  They are called  Swedged Radius Rods.  They are made of aluminum with the ends compressed for more strength.  Straight rods are weaker at the threads.  On the ends there are left and right threaded Heim Ends.  There are several grades of these.  The aluminum ones that are pictured are the best.  They actually have a teflon race and are pretty much garrenteed not to wear out like steel heims.  They are sold at race car shops that deal mostly in dirt cars.  They come in all diameters and lengths.  If you have trouble locating them email me and i'll find some websites for you.||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-18-2001||05:11 AM||||All thread, strut rod tubes, trailing arms, Swedged Radius Rods   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Makes perfect sense now!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Thanks for the tips on places to purchase, I'm becoming a little wiser quickly here! (you guys rock!)<P>Lizzy, the NHBB ends I'm using are actually all stainless/Teflon (even the big threaded end is stainless steel, 410 I belive...) At anyrate, they are said to be the very finest available, and I do know they are used on the suspension members in Formula 1 GP cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Should be strong enough for a road car's suspension then &lt;g&gt;<P>I'll keep a heads up for the Swedged (compressed)rods, thanks for the tip!<P>Any other good vendors of quality Swedged rods?  I'd like to see wall thickness, stregenth info, etc.  <P>Thanks for the tip on UB Macine, I'll call them and talk their ear off, then buy a bunch of their stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
